        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): suppress progress chrome sends",
        "body": "## Summary\n- detect progress-only Slack tool chrome payloads with leading tool emoji plus command/status body\n- convert thread-scoped chrome to reactions instead of `chat.postMessage`\n- fail closed by suppressing chrome without a reaction target while preserving semantic replies\n\n## What Problem This Solves\nProgress-only operational chrome like `:hammer_and_wrench: `pnpm test`` or `:writing_hand: Write: MEMORY.md` can leak into Slack as user-visible messages when a tool/status payload accidentally reaches the Slack send path. This creates noise in working channels and violates the progress-chrome pre-send gate. The Slack extension now classifies only narrow progress-only payloads and prevents them from becoming chat posts.\n\n## Evidence\n- `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false vitest run --project extension-slack extensions/slack/src/send.identity-fallback.test.ts extensions/slack/src/send.blocks.test.ts extensions/slack/src/action-runtime.test.ts` passed (3 files, 128 tests)\n- `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false tsgo:extensions` passed\n- `CI=true pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false oxfmt --check extensions/slack/src/send.ts extensions/slack/src/send.identity-fallback.test.ts` passed\n- `git diff --check` passed\n\n## Live Slack Proof\nGenerated against the TCG Slack API from the PR branch code on 2026-07-09 23:35 UTC, before the no-conflict rebase to refreshed head `9901e6fc70f`. Channel is redacted; it was the Jack bot App Home/DM proof surface, not a client or public channel.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"workspace\": \"The Casely Group\",\n  \"botUser\": \"U0AUPGF8GRF\",\n  \"channel\": \"D***07U3\",\n  \"anchorTs\": \"1783640151.091679\",\n  \"threadProgressChrome\": {\n    \"input\": \":hammer_and_wrench: `pnpm test`\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"messageId\": \"suppressed\",\n      \"suppressed\": true\n    },\n    \"anchorReactionNames\": [\"hammer_and_wrench\"]\n  },\n  \"noThreadProgressChrome\": {\n    \"input\": \":writing_hand: Write: MEMORY.md\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"messageId\": \"suppressed\",\n      \"suppressed\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"semanticReply\": {\n    \"input\": \":hammer_and_wrench: I ran `pnpm test` and it passed\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"messageId\": \"1783640151.421249\",\n      \"suppressed\": false,\n      \"threadTs\": \"1783640151.091679\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"redactedThreadTranscript\": [\n    {\n      \"ts\": \"1783640151.091679\",\n      \"text\": \"Slack progress-chrome guard live proof anchor 2026-07-09T23:35:50.946Z\",\n      \"reactions\": [\"hammer_and_wrench\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ts\": \"1783640151.421249\",\n      \"text\": \":hammer_and_wrench: I ran `pnpm test` and it passed\",\n      \"reactions\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Verification\n- Thread-scoped progress chrome converts to `reactions.add` instead of `chat.postMessage`.\n- Progress chrome without a reaction target is suppressed before Slack post.\n- Semantic replies using the same leading emoji and an embedded backticked command remain sendable, including without final sentence punctuation.\n",
        "branch": "jack/slack-progress-chrome-guard-v2",
